name: Partial saved results lead with warnings before long paths, retain full details and survive restart
size: 120x36
cwd: @TARGET
require-env: KUZUSHI_DEVEX_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/replay_hierarchy.py seed @TARGET @ART
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: run codeql:scan {"threads":0}
require-live-snap: 20 threads | rejected-option
paste-file: @ART/replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Recorded warning | partial-warning
expect: Outcome · partial
ask: Does the saved result clearly separate its partial status, recorded warning, unknown cost and original summary without inventing a new verdict or recommendation?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: partial-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: partial-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: partial-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: partial-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Recorded warning | warning-first-40x12
expect: Outcome · partial
expect: ERROR
expect: cost not recorded
keys: NPage
live-snap: warning-next-page-40x12
keys: Home
live-snap: warning-home-40x12
ask: Is the limitation visible in the first compact frame, with working paging/back controls and the retained alert still present?
keys: End
live-snap: complete-receipt-tail-40x12
resize: 120x36
keys: Home
type: held draft
keys: C-b C-b C-b
resize: 40x12
keys: NPage PPage
resize: 120x36
type: X
require-live-snap: 20 held drXaft | cursor-preserved
keys: End C-u
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/replay_hierarchy.py preserved @TARGET @ART
ask: Does full receipt access and resize preserve the exact draft/cursor without rerunning analysis or changing source, findings or earlier receipts?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Recorded warning | recovered-warning
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Recorded warning | recovered-40x12
expect: Outcome · partial
expect: cost not recorded
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/replay_hierarchy.py restart @TARGET @ART
ask: Does no-color restart restore the partial result and warning while preserving exact historical data and avoiding phase completion or new work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
